==Sanskrit==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sa|inc-pro|*Háikas}}, from {{inh|sa|iir-pro|*Háykas}}, from {{inh|sa|ine-pro|*óynos|*(H)óykos|one, single}}. Cognates include {{cog|itc-ola|oinos}} (Classical {{cog|la|ūnus}}), {{cog|grc|οἶος}} and {{cog|ang|ān}} ({{cog|en|one}} and {{m|en|an}}). {{rfv-etymology|lang=sa}}

===Pronunciation===
{{sa-IPA|a=1}}

===Numeral===
{{head|sa|numeral|tr=éka}}

# [[one]]

===Adjective===
{{sa-adj|tr=éka}}

# (with and without {{m|sa|tr=eva|एव}}) [[alone]], [[solitary]], [[single]], happening only once, that one only
# the [[same]], one and the same, [[identical]]
# one of two or many
# single of its kind, [[unique]], [[singular]], [[chief]], pre-eminent, [[excellent]]
# [[sincere]], [[truthful]]
# [[little]], [[small]]
# (sometimes used as an indefinite article), [[a]], [[an]]

===Noun===
